1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,420
Fleet tools need credentials by name, and

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,591
they need somewhere sensible to keep them.

3
00:00:06,591 --> 00:00:12,111
Lazarette Lite is the light answer:
a browser window on the Windows

4
00:00:12,111 --> 00:00:16,575
Credential Manager you already have,
with no new vault.

5
00:00:16,575 --> 00:00:20,651
This is a short run,
using throwaway credentials only.

6
00:00:21,401 --> 00:00:24,933
Lazarette Lite is a browser window
on the Windows Credential Manager.

7
00:00:24,933 --> 00:00:30,217
Double-click the launcher, and a small
PowerShell server starts on this computer.

8
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:35,890
The server listens on loopback only,
on a port Windows picks.

9
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:41,058
It answers only your own Windows user's
processes, with a one-time launch token

10
00:00:41,058 --> 00:00:42,415
and a session cookie.

11
00:00:43,115 --> 00:00:45,584
The secrets themselves stay in Windows

12
00:00:45,584 --> 00:00:49,573
Credential Manager, as ordinary
generic entries under a prefix.

13
00:00:49,573 --> 00:00:52,041
Lite ships no vault of its own.

14
00:00:52,741 --> 00:00:56,500
Fleet tools reach them through a loader
that answers to the

15
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,635
same command names as Lazarette:
get a secret by service and user.

16
00:01:01,335 --> 00:01:04,372
What Lite does not do: custom fields,

17
00:01:04,372 --> 00:01:07,649
or Lazarette's key sharing with Fairlead.

18
00:01:07,649 --> 00:01:10,305
That stays with the full Lazarette.

19
00:01:11,005 --> 00:01:14,454
Safety:
secrets stay hidden until you reveal them,

20
00:01:14,454 --> 00:01:18,511
delete asks first,
and nothing outside its prefix is listed.

21
00:01:18,761 --> 00:01:21,798
First, add a credential in the browser.

22
00:01:21,798 --> 00:01:26,175
Service fleet-tools, user demo,
and a secret I made up for this demo.

23
00:01:26,175 --> 00:01:31,364
The field masks it as it's typed,
and none of it is a real password. Save.

24
00:01:31,503 --> 00:01:34,827
Saved, and it's already in
Windows Credential Manager.

25
00:01:34,827 --> 00:01:37,512
The secret stays hidden
until someone clicks Reveal.

26
00:01:37,512 --> 00:01:39,606
Here it is, blurred for the recording,

27
00:01:39,606 --> 00:01:42,290
because even a throwaway
doesn't belong on screen.

28
00:01:42,882 --> 00:01:44,851
Now a Fleet tool asks for it by name.

29
00:01:44,851 --> 00:01:48,210
This is a short stand-in script,
not a real tool.

30
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:52,657
It loads Lazarette the way the real
ones do, and Start-LiteFleet points

31
00:01:52,657 --> 00:01:53,892
that loader at Lite.

32
00:01:54,592 --> 00:01:57,803
It gets the secret: fifteen characters.

33
00:01:57,803 --> 00:01:59,241
The value is never printed.

34
00:01:59,941 --> 00:02:01,494
Now a name Lite doesn't hold.

35
00:02:01,494 --> 00:02:03,600
It refuses with a plain error.

36
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:07,660
It never guesses,
and it never hands back an empty password,

37
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:11,255
so a tool fails early instead of running
with nothing.

38
00:02:11,255 --> 00:02:12,625
Now the evidence trail.

39
00:02:12,625 --> 00:02:17,371
Get-LiteItemNames returns names only,
never a secret.

40
00:02:17,371 --> 00:02:19,926
And this is the whole data store:

41
00:02:19,926 --> 00:02:24,133
an ordinary generic entry in
Windows Credential Manager.

42
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:27,670
I also made a second throwaway
entry outside Lite's prefix.

43
00:02:27,670 --> 00:02:31,797
Windows has it, you can see it here,
and Lite's list never showed it.

44
00:02:31,797 --> 00:02:35,066
Lite only reads
and writes entries under its own prefix.

45
00:02:35,766 --> 00:02:37,450
Cleanup belongs in the trail too.

46
00:02:37,450 --> 00:02:42,189
Delete asks you to confirm first,
then the credential is removed from

47
00:02:42,189 --> 00:02:45,980
Windows Credential Manager,
and the list is empty again.

48
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:49,970
Quit ends the session and the server
stops. Nothing was left running.

49
00:02:50,177 --> 00:02:54,487
That is Lazarette Lite:
named credentials for Fleet tools,

50
00:02:54,487 --> 00:02:59,163
from the Credential Manager you
already have, with no new vault.

51
00:02:59,163 --> 00:03:04,351
Everything you saw ran for real on
this PC, with throwaway credentials

52
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:05,885
that are now deleted.

53
00:03:05,885 --> 00:03:09,099
The only stand-in was
the short tool script.

54
00:03:09,099 --> 00:03:12,136
Custom fields and Lazarette's key sharing

55
00:03:12,136 --> 00:03:16,113
with Fairlead stay
with the full Lazarette. Fair winds.

